From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:55:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] board: qualcomm: add the Eliza MTP and CQS EVK

The Eliza MTP and the Eliza CQS EVK can boot with TF-A and OP-TEE in
place of the vendor UEFI firmware, with U-Boot as BL33. TF-A passes
U-Boot no device tree, so the board's device tree is built in, selected
with DEVICE_TREE= on the make command line as for the other TF-A
boards; everything else the boards need is enabled by qcom_defconfig
and tfa-optee.config.

Document how to build and boot both boards, add a debug-eliza.config
fragment for the early debug UART as other Snapdragon SoCs have, and
add a maintainer entry for Eliza.

[port: this base's board/qualcomm/tfa-optee.config does not enable
 OPTEE_LIB; a standalone build for OP-TEE needs CONFIG_OPTEE_LIB=y as
 well (the meta-qcom recipe's tfa-optee.cfg sets it)]

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
